    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> are mixed with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. At equilibrium for the reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8652;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> are formed, the equilibrium constant for the reaction will be,",
